{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/598980-vampire-stories","id":598980,"title":"vampire stories","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-21T20:54:15-07:00","id":598980,"title":"vampire stories","content":"Hello, I am looking for stories written based around vampire the requiem. These could be fan made or official products. Would anyone have any recommendations or suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6947-cubleds","name":"cubleds","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T21:08:29-07:00","id":599005,"title":"","content":"Have you read <a href=\"http://www.drivethrufiction.com/product/117396/The-Strix-Chronicle-Anthology\" target=\"_blank\">The Strix Chronicle Anthology</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T23:30:37-07:00","id":599058,"title":"","content":"I am currently going through it, and it is giving me a far better idea of how too handle strix in my chronicles. I am actually trying too work on a particular flaw of my games by looking for examples in fiction. I have a bad habit of making my cities too tidy, their governments too logical and their kindred too agreeable, sensible, and generally have too much common sense too have things going wrong at the rate that they should be. I legitimately have trouble coming up with bad idea that would make sense for a character too attempt. Also getting a proper grip on how the city can function while caught somewhere in cold war and bloody street fighting.<br /> <br /> So I suppose I am hoping too get a better grip on how too play into the bad ideas kindred are expected too have. ying levels of cold war/ block by bloody block stru","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6947-cubleds","name":"cubleds","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T02:16:30-07:00","id":599098,"title":"","content":"Put your NPCs with mutually exclusive goals. Bishop Birch wants to have everyone go to the Sanctum mass. Hierophant Mahala has quite a few problems with that. Carthians want to establish a better life in the slum neighbourhood, so that it's easier for them to feed, but the Invictus lords want to promote their own businesses, which means they must keep abusing the neighbourhood. And this is just a very big view of covenants. Ancillae Johnson has the neighborhood to himself for the past ten years. Neonate Tom's touchstone and still living mother is living in the neighbourhood. She's also stubborn as all hell in her desire to keep living in his house. Johnson wants to keep his lands, Tom wants to keep his mom safe and accessible to him. Johnson forbids other vampires from entering his domain. <br /> <br /> You can't have tidy if different people want different mutually exclusive things. One of them get's what they want, the other is plotting how to get what he wants and so forever the Danse Macabre spins. <br /> <br /> Couple that with the fact that NPCs don't know everything and chaos will ensue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T05:43:17-07:00","id":599245,"title":"","content":"Remember to make most vampires as selfish as you can. They can't realy let it go. They WILL have everything they want in the future, so any agreement is doomed in the long course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T07:25:32-07:00","id":599361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cubleds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/598980-vampire-stories?p=599058#post599058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am currently going through it, and it is giving me a far better idea of how too handle strix in my chronicles. I am actually trying too work on a particular flaw of my games by looking for examples in fiction. I have a bad habit of making my cities too tidy, their governments too logical and their kindred too agreeable, sensible, and generally have too much common sense too have things going wrong at the rate that they should be. I legitimately have trouble coming up with bad idea that would make sense for a character too attempt. Also getting a proper grip on how the city can function while caught somewhere in cold war and bloody street fighting.<br /> <br /> So I suppose I am hoping too get a better grip on how too play into the bad ideas kindred are expected too have. ying levels of cold war/ block by bloody block stru</div> </div> </div> </div>For inspiration you might try looking up some Noir fiction, or even just the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/FilmNoir\" target=\"_blank\">tropes associated with it</a>. I'd also say stop trying to make things characters do always &quot;make sense&quot;, instead give the character an irrational flaw (extremely greedy, bigoted against a certain clan, selfish to a fault, etc.) then keep their actions consistently &quot;in character&quot;. You can invent something in the character's history to justify their flaw (came from poverty, a Gangrel killed their sire, etc.) but you can assign the flaw arbitrarily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","user":"Vyrkolash","date":". 07-22-2015, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T10:58:18-07:00","id":599640,"title":"","content":"Thank you. I should say I have been able too do competing organizations. (In the city Carthian of Los Angeles I am building has the lacea sanctum tasked enforcing a no crone allowed law. I also have an invictus faction based out of the mexican cartels growing taking over the street crime.) Most of my conflicts are either from an outside force, or are large scale things that will only come too ahead after maney maney sessions, and 13 sessions of quiet peace dose not an interested player make.<br /> <br /> The advice you have been giving me has been helpfull because i suffer on the problems of conflicts on the scale of individual kindred. I will try too impliment what you have said so that even in a faction of two people it is not a completely unified front.<br /> <br /> I was having a problem with the minor conflicts because with the factions helping eachother it seemed like a WW1 situation where any spark would set everything off. Which in turn lead too the thought in my head of &quot;why would this person think it was worth it too piss off those people&quot; but you guys are right vampires are gennerally obsessive and irrational. I dont want a city that is either in perfect balance or having a night of long knives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6947,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6947-cubleds","user":"cubleds","date":". 07-22-2015, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6947-cubleds","name":"cubleds","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T12:13:17-07:00","id":599689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cubleds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/598980-vampire-stories?p=599640#post599640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you. I should say I have been able too do competing organizations. (In the city Carthian of Los Angeles I am building has the lacea sanctum tasked enforcing a no crone allowed law. I also have an invictus faction based out of the mexican cartels growing taking over the street crime.) Most of my conflicts are either from an outside force, or are large scale things that will only come too ahead after maney maney sessions, and 13 sessions of quiet peace dose not an interested player make.<br /> <br /> The advice you have been giving me has been helpfull because i suffer on the problems of conflicts on the scale of individual kindred. I will try too impliment what you have said so that even in a faction of two people it is not a completely unified front.<br /> <br /> I was having a problem with the minor conflicts because with the factions helping eachother it seemed like a WW1 situation where any spark would set everything off. Which in turn lead too the thought in my head of &quot;why would this person think it was worth it too piss off those people&quot; but you guys are right vampires are gennerally obsessive and irrational. I dont want a city that is either in perfect balance or having a night of long knives.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing to also keep in mind is that large-scale events don't just happen. Let me give you an example from a chronicle I'm currently running.<br /> Alecto, in Athens, is governed by a secretive cabal of elders (few know of their existence): the Inner Circle (a group of Ventrue that survived, not only the purge, but even greater disasters in Athenian history). They want to discredit Ypochreosi to the point that the Kindred of Athens <i>demand</i> that a tyrant seizes power to protect them and the city's prosperity.<br /> <br /> To do this, Alecto slowly creeps in with the local media and financial corporations. On the larger scale of things, they do this through the powerful mortal capitalist dynasties they control. A firm with innovative security solutions (including facial and GPS tracking) is acquired by the Bobolas conglomerate (traditionally involved in media). If the Sheriff or the secret police of Ypochreosi are clever enough, they'll start snooping around the takeover.<br /> <br /> On a smaller scale, a journalist known for his network of whistleblowers and anti-corruption investigative work, goes missing. This is a small but crucial step in someone's grand plot. Then there's that trespassing incident in the Pendeli underground government facilities. Supposedly, they've been abandoned since the 1980s. Why is everyone freaking out, then? Perhaps because a certain valuable relic belonging to Aegis kai Doru (whose armory and reliquary is located beneath Pendeli Mountain) was stolen during the break-in. Urban explorers? Sure, if you believe the mainstream media, now controlled by Alecto.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T19:38:30-07:00","id":601319,"title":"","content":"<i>A Hunger Like Fire </i>and <i>The Marriage of Virtue and Viciousness</i> are my favorites. The story from those two novels ends its first season in the chapter fiction for <i>The Danse Macabre</i>, and there's a prequel in <i>The Strix Chronicle Anthology</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 07-23-2015, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T20:58:09-07:00","id":601361,"title":"","content":"Lullay, Lullay is powerful, deeply touching and disturbing at the same time. The Strix Anthology is full of worthwhile stories, but that's my favorite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T21:32:23-07:00","id":601377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/598980-vampire-stories?p=601361#post601361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lullay, Lullay is powerful, deeply touching and disturbing at the same time. The Strix Anthology is full of worthwhile stories, but that's my favorite.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We revisit those characters in <i>Secrets of the Covenants</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T12:03:31-07:00","id":622492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/598980-vampire-stories?p=601361#post601361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lullay, Lullay is powerful, deeply touching and disturbing at the same time. The Strix Anthology is full of worthwhile stories, but that's my favorite.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why thank you. I'm rather fond of Little Red and that big, goonish ghoul (whose name I'm always forgetting, but he was in that one B-movie...remember?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#990000\">Joshua Alan Doetsch</span></b><br /> <b>Freelance Writer<br /> <a href=\"http://joshuadoetsch.com/\" target=\"_blank\">joshuadoetsch.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1054-scrivnomancer","name":"scrivnomancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1054_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T12:10:00-07:00","id":622502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/598980-vampire-stories?p=601361#post601361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lullay, Lullay is powerful, deeply touching and disturbing at the same time. The Strix Anthology is full of worthwhile stories, but that's my favorite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lullay, Lullay isn't just a great story, it's also a great demonstration of characters suffering the depredations of a Strix and eventually overcoming it. It's perfect for the Anthology and pretty essential reading for a Vampire ST, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}